# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — never commit. The bare `.env` rule plus the wildcard below is
# deliberate belt-and-braces: `.env.local`, `.env.production` etc. are also
# blocked, while `.env.example` is explicitly re-allowed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
secrets.toml
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/

# Personal working notes that live alongside the project but are not part of it.
# Office lock files (~$...) must never be committed.
*.docx
*.doc
*.xlsx
*.pptx
~$*

# Private interview preparation -- kept locally, never published.
INTERVIEW_GUIDE.md
docs/PRESENTATION_OUTLINE.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data policy — READ BEFORE EDITING
#
# data/raw/ and data/processed/ are COMMITTED on purpose. They are what make
# the app open with no API key and no network access, which the live demo
# depends on. Do not add them here.
#
# The only data excluded is the local LLM response cache (a working artifact,
# regenerable, and potentially large) and one reader's own label corrections,
# which are local review state rather than project data -- committing them
# would ship one person's edits to everyone who clones the repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/cache/
data/processed/overrides.json
*.tmp

# Removed from the public repo by request; kept locally only.
docs/DESIGN_ANSWERS.md
